    "collapsible_content_hzCe49": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "text_block_YDC9Fg": {
          "type": "text-block",
          "settings": {
            "block_heading": "Where do your Chinese New Year Plants come from?",
            "block_heading_tag": "h4",
            "text": "<p>Our Chinese New Year plants come from both Mainland China and Malaysia!</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_block_LGmX7n": {
          "type": "text-block",
          "settings": {
            "block_heading": "What are some lucky plants to purchase for the Year of the Snake?",
            "block_heading_tag": "h4",
            "text": "<p>Every Chinese New Year plant carries its own auspicious meaning, so you can’t go wrong with choosing one that you like!</p><p>For the Year of the Snake, consider purchasing a Sansevieria, also known as the Snake Plant. This plant is believed to bring health and wealth, making it a perfect choice for this zodiac year.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_block_NGd6Gc": {
          "type": "text-block",
          "settings": {
            "block_heading": "Do Chinese New Year plants and flowers bloom all year round?",
            "block_heading_tag": "h4",
            "text": "<p>Chinese New Year plants and flowers, like other plants, do not bloom all year round. These plants are typically cultivated to bloom during the Chinese New Year period. It is normal for their flowers to shed after this period, and certain species, such as Azaleas, may rarely bloom due to Singapore’s tropical climate.</p><p>Since these plants are grown to flower around Chinese New Year, they may not arrive with flowers if delivered early. To increase the chances of blooming, ensure your plant receives sufficient sunlight and water every day. For more care tips, refer to the product description of the plants you ordered or reach out to us at via email at <a href=\"mailto:thegreencorner@prince.com.sg\">thegreencorner@prince.com.sg</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_block_kBF3Qa": {
          "type": "text-block",
          "settings": {
            "block_heading": "How do I care for Chinese New Year plants?",
            "block_heading_tag": "h4",
            "text": "<p>Caring for Chinese New Year plants is relatively simple. Here are some tips for different types of plants:</p><p>Flowering Plants (e.g., Celosia and Cockscomb): Ensure they receive bright and direct sunlight throughout the day. Water them daily as they are exposed to the sun to keep the soil moist.</p><p>Fruiting Plants (e.g., Mandarin Oranges and Four Season Kumquats): Place them where they can receive morning sun (east) and afternoon shade to prevent excessive fruit drop. Water them daily to prevent the soil from drying out.</p><p>For more detailed care tips, refer to the product description of the plants you ordered or reach out to us via email at <a href=\"mailto:thegreencorner@prince.com.sg\">thegreencorner@prince.com.sg</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_block_xxzQKc": {
          "type": "text-block",
          "settings": {
            "block_heading": "Do the Chinese New Year plants come with decorations?",
            "block_heading_tag": "h4",
            "text": "<p>Our Chinese New Year plants do not come with decorations.</p><p>However, we offer pussy-willow arrangements that are beautifully decorated by our design specialists, perfect as a gift to enhance your Chinese New Year celebrations.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_block_cPy3BF": {
          "type": "text-block",
          "settings": {
            "block_heading": "Can I visit your retail store to purchase Chinese New Year plants?",
            "block_heading_tag": "h4",
            "text": "<p>Yes, you most definitely can! Visit our retail outlet located at 3A Lor Ah Thia, Singapore 679278, during our opening hours to purchase our Chinese New Year plants. For more information, follow us on Facebook or Instagram <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/thegreencornersg/\" target=\"_blank\">@thegreencornersg</a> or email us at <a href=\"mailto:thegreencorner@prince.com.sg\">thegreencorner@prince.com.sg</a> for updates.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_block_UXqYkk": {
          "type": "text-block",
          "settings": {
            "block_heading": "Can I self-collect my Chinese New Year plants?",
            "block_heading_tag": "h4",
            "text": "<p>Yes, you can! When you place an order online at thegreencorner.com.sg, you can select the self-collect option. You will receive an automated email once your order is ready for collection.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_block_KiHXJ8": {
          "type": "text-block",
          "settings": {
            "block_heading": "Do you offer disposal services for Chinese New Year plants?",
            "block_heading_tag": "h4",
            "text": "<p>Here can be a brief overview of the information available in this section, explaining its purpose and how users can interact with it.</p>"
          }
